      "rule": "R2",
      "severity": "should",
      "text": "The docstring of `Resolved.Query.productions_copyOf` says the law holds for \"the productions of {name}`Resolved.Query.copyOf`\", but the formula covers only the copy query whose width is the source table's column count (`copyOf position table.shape.columns.length names`), so a reader can take it as true for any width. Fix: say that the law is about the copy query at that position whose width is the number of columns of the source table, so it selects all of the table's columns."
    }
